<section class="vx-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <h1 class="vx-hero-product" id="hero-title">vexes</h1>
    <div class="vx-hero-badge">npm v{{ versions.vexes.version }} · source v{{ versions.vexes.sourceVersion }} · experimental</div>
    <p class="vx-hero-tagline">Dependency evidence without pretending it is a verdict</p>
    <p class="vx-hero-desc">vexes is an experimental local CLI that matches dependencies against OSV advisories and surfaces heuristic npm/PyPI supply-chain evidence for human review. It supports ten ecosystems for advisory scanning, emits JSON and SARIF, and has no external runtime npm dependencies. It is pre-1.0, has not been externally audited, and is not proven to stop real-world attacks.</p>
    <div class="vx-hero-actions">
      <a href="https://github.com/penumbraforge/vexes" class="vx-btn vx-btn-outline" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Source and current README</a>
