<section class="vx-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Quick Start</div>
    <h2 id="install-title">Run the published package</h2>
    <pre class="vx-pre"><code><span class="code-comment"># npm latest is currently v{{ versions.vexes.version }}</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> <span class="code-cmd">npx</span> <span class="code-arg">@penumbraforge/vexes scan</span>

<span class="code-comment"># Or use the current v{{ versions.vexes.sourceVersion }} source tree</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> <span class="code-cmd">git clone</span> <span class="code-arg">https://github.com/penumbraforge/vexes.git</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> <span class="code-cmd">node</span> <span class="code-arg">vexes/bin/vexes.js scan --path /path/to/project</span></code></pre>
    <div class="vx-note">Requires Node.js {{ versions.vexes.node }}+. No account is required. Normal scans send package coordinates to OSV; analysis may contact registries and download bounded package samples. Optional AI modes send sanitized finding data to the endpoint you configure.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Scope</div>
    <h2 id="scope-title">What it does—and what it does not prove</h2>
    <div class="vx-features-grid vx-features-grid--pairs" role="list">
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>OSV advisory matches</h3>
        <p><code>scan</code> enumerates supported dependency records and asks OSV whether an exact version falls in an affected range. A match is evidence of an upstream advisory, not proof that the vulnerable path is reachable or exploited.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Bounded heuristic analysis</h3>
        <p><code>analyze</code> uses available npm/PyPI registry data and selected source samples to flag install hooks, risky patterns, publisher or timing changes, typosquat-like names, and capability changes. Individual layers run only when the ecosystem and evidence support them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Visible incompleteness</h3>
        <p>Coverage gaps and failed requested stages are reported as incomplete and normally exit 2. Exit 0 means the requested supported checks completed with no finding at the active threshold; it is not a safety guarantee.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Machine-readable output</h3>
        <p>Successful command paths use a versioned JSON envelope, and scans can emit SARIF. Command-specific payloads still differ, and a few early/setup/watch paths are not yet a uniform contract.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="engine-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Heuristic Analysis</div>
    <h2 id="engine-title">Four evidence groups, where supported</h2>
    <p>These groups organize npm/PyPI analysis. They are not four checks applied to every dependency in every ecosystem.</p>
    <div class="vx-features-grid vx-features-grid--pairs" role="list">
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>1 — Source patterns</h3>
        <p>Vendored Acorn parses selected JavaScript; selected Python files use pattern matching. Matches cover code execution, process spawning, credentials, networking, obfuscation, and dynamic loading. Legitimate code can match.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>2 — Dependency metadata</h3>
        <p>For analyzed npm releases, profiles newly added dependencies for age, sparse metadata, same-publisher staging, consumer install hooks, and similarity to a curated package-name list.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>3 — Capability change</h3>
        <p>When usable previous-version data exists, compares observable install-hook capabilities. Without a real previous-version comparison it reports an initial dangerous capability instead of claiming escalation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>4 — Registry metadata</h3>
        <p>Reviews publish timing, maintainers, dormant-package activity, repository fields, and decoded attestation identity fields. It does not cryptographically verify DSSE signatures, certificates, or transparency-log proofs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

