<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="eco-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Inputs</div>
    <h2 id="eco-title">{{ versions.vexes.ecosystems }} OSV ecosystems</h2>
    <p>Resolved lockfiles are preferred. Some manifest fallbacks provide exact pins but not a resolved graph and are marked incomplete. Unsupported or malformed shapes fail visibly rather than becoming an empty “clean” scan.</p>
    <div class="vx-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Supported dependency inputs">
      <table class="vx-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Ecosystem</th><th scope="col">Recognized inputs</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>npm</td><td>package-lock.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, yarn.lock</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PyPI</td><td>Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cargo</td><td>Cargo.lock</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Go</td><td>go.mod preferred; go.sum fallback</td></tr>
          <tr><td>RubyGems</td><td>Gemfile.lock</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Composer</td><td>composer.lock</td></tr>
          <tr><td>NuGet</td><td>packages.lock.json; project-file fallback</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Java</td><td>gradle.lockfile; pom.xml fallback</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hex</td><td>mix.lock</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dart/pub</td><td>pubspec.lock</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="commands-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Commands</div>
    <h2 id="commands-title">{{ versions.vexes.commands }} primary commands</h2>
    <div class="vx-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Vexes commands">
      <table class="vx-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">Current role</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>scan</code></td><td>Enumerate supported dependencies and query OSV</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>analyze</code></td><td>Review bounded npm/PyPI heuristic evidence; <code>--deep</code> downloads selected samples</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>fix</code></td><td>Show npm upgrade candidates for which OSV returned no match at lookup time; rescan and test them</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>guard</code></td><td>Experimental explicit public-npm install assessment; supports narrow <code>npm install/i/add</code> grammar only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>monitor</code></td><td>CI or watch-mode scans; watch mode is early work</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>explain</code></td><td>Opt-in model-assisted triage using a configured local or hosted endpoint</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>inspect</code></td><td>Inspect one npm/PyPI coordinate with the evidence available for it</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>doctor</code></td><td>Report runtime, parser-fixture, cache, and optional isolation support</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>licenses</code></td><td>Inventory declared dependency licenses; not legal advice</td></tr>
        </tbody>
